WEBVTT

00:19:58.288 --> 00:20:03.038
and sort of commit to it for now and sort
of see where it goes. And Matt.

00:20:03.913 --> 00:20:06.913
To his great credit, and it's one of the
reasons I love working with him,

00:20:06.913 --> 00:20:11.121
is he's someone who really wants to
stop and examine and consider

00:20:11.121 --> 00:20:14.621
and reconsider it and look at it from all
sides and see if there's a better way.

00:20:14.621 --> 00:20:17.913
And can it go deeper and can it be, you
know, can it be more emotional?

00:20:18.038 --> 00:20:21.663
And I think that that, you know, part
of that is probably, you know,

00:20:21.663 --> 00:20:25.704
less about thinking and rethinking and
more about my being more impatient.

00:20:25.704 --> 00:20:30.329
And when we work together, we had our
offices right next to each other.